  "_comment": "The text rules of docs/mcp-enclave.md section 17.10, as vectors for the archive server (internal/mcpauth/textrules.go) and the enclave (enclave/send/textrules.mjs). text is JSON as a reader receives it, every character outside printable ASCII escaped; read it exactly (a lone surrogate escape must not become U+FFFD). draft is why the rules refuse it in a draft, self why in an own-chat or direct send (which also refuse links), null when it passes. The text is checked after CR LF and CR become LF, for, in this order: control characters (C0 but tab and newline, DEL, C1, a lone surrogate), then text-direction controls (U+202A to U+202E, U+2066 to U+2069), then empty after trimming white space as JavaScript's trim() does, then links. Every other character is kept; the console marks the invisible ones.",
